  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since in azulene (IV) two rings share a double bond, therefore, two electrons of this double bond can be counted towards each. As a result, each ring has  <math><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> -electrons and hence azulene is aromatic. Pyrrole (II), the two double bonds + one lone pair of electrons on the N atom).",
